-- title:
--   H AConsistency Submeas From Line Consistency Of Axis Self
-- statement:
--   **Vertical-line consistency yields point consistency for a polynomial submeasurement.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `strategy` be a symmetric successor strategy, and let $H$ have degree-bounded polynomial outcomes. Let $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta$ be errors, with the axis and self-consistency hypotheses supplied by `haxis` and `hself_good`, and let `hline` give the vertical-line `ConsRel` bound. For $k\in\mathbb{N}$ with $1\le k$,
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{ConsRel}_{\mathrm{strategy.state}}\left(\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^{m+1}),\operatorname{strategy.pointMeasurement},\operatorname{polynomialEvaluationFamily}(\mathrm{params.next},H),\operatorname{ldPastingInInductionNu}(\mathrm{params},k,\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta)\right).
--   $$
--
--   The proof transports the line relation, evaluates at the final coordinate, applies the axis and self-consistency comparison, and uses `hAConsistency_error_le_nu_of_pos`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.hAConsistency_submeas_from_lineConsistency_of_axis_self`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
